{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Ordinal.Arithmetic","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Ordinal.Family","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Ordinal.NaturalOps","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.ConditionallyCompleteLattice.Basic"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.sub","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L416-L421","doc":"Subtraction of infinitesimals is infinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite.sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite.sub","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L410-L414","doc":"Subtraction of finite surreals is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite.neg","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L404-L408","doc":"Negation preserves finiteness (using the same bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.one_isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.one_isFinite","kind":"theorem","line":399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L399-L402","doc":"`1` is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.zero_isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.zero_isFinite","kind":"theorem","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L394-L397","doc":"`0` is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.isFinite_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.isFinite_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L379-L385","doc":"A finite surreal is the sum of a real and an infinitesimal.\nThe real is unique (= the standard part). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.isFinite_has_standardPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.isFinite_has_standardPart","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L313-L377","doc":"A finite surreal has an associated real (its standard part).\n\n**Construction**: `r = sup { q ∈ ℝ | ofReal q ≤ x }`.  Existence\nuses Dedekind completeness of ℝ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.standardPart_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.standardPart_unique","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L289-L311","doc":"Uniqueness of the real part of a finite surreal: if two reals\nboth differ from `x` by an infinitesimal, they are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.mul_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.mul_finite","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L227-L287","doc":"Finite × infinitesimal is infinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite.mul","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L212-L225","doc":"Product of two finite surreals is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite.add","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L202-L210","doc":"Sum of two finite surreals is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.add","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L184-L200","doc":"Sum of two infinitesimals is infinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.neg","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L177-L182","doc":"Negation of an infinitesimal is infinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.ofReal_isInfinitesimal_iff_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.ofReal_isInfinitesimal_iff_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L157-L175","doc":"A real is infinitesimal in `K` iff it is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.ofReal_abs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.ofReal_abs","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L146-L155","doc":"The image of `ofReal` commutes with `abs`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.zero_isInfinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.zero_isInfinitesimal","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L139-L144","doc":"Zero is infinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal.isFinite","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L130-L137","doc":"An infinitesimal is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsInfinitesimal","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L125-L128","doc":"A surreal `x` is **infinitesimal** if it is bounded by every\npositive real. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.IsFinite","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L121-L123","doc":"A surreal `x` is **finite** if it is bounded by some natural number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toAlgebra","kind":"instance","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L109-L115","doc":"Every `SurrealField K` is canonically an `Algebra ℝ K` via the\n`ofReal` ring homomorphism.  This unlocks Mathlib's\n`Polynomial.aeval`, `MvPolynomial.aeval`, and the full\n`Algebra`-flavored API for free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.instCoeRealOfSurrealField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.instCoeRealOfSurrealField","kind":"instance","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L105-L107","doc":"Coerce a real into the surreal field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.omegaSurreal_gt_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.omegaSurreal_gt_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L103-L103","doc":"`omegaSurreal` is strictly greater than every natural number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.omegaSurreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.omegaSurreal","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The first infinite surreal `ω` as an element of `K`.\n\nConway's construction: `ω = {0, 1, 2, … | }`.  Its existence\nin any `SurrealField K` follows from `K` extending the ordinals\nvia the canonical inclusion (Ehrlich 2012, Thm 12.5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_ofReal_le_omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_ofReal_le_omega","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Real numbers have birthday at most ω. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_avg_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_avg_le","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L92-L92","doc":"Birthday of a dyadic midpoint is bounded by the natural-sum\nof its parents' birthdays plus one.\n\nThis is exactly Conway's `{L | R}` recipe: the midpoint\n`(x + y) / 2` is born one day after the deepest of `x, y`.\nThe bound is genuinely independent of `birthday_add_le`: the\nadditive bound gives only upper bounds on `birthday (x + y)`\n(hence lower bounds on summands), whereas this asks for an\nupper bound on a *strictly earlier* surreal.\n\n**Narrow kernel rationale.**  Every caller in the surreals\nappendix that reasons about halving does so in the form\n`(parent₁ + parent₂) / 2` (Gonshor sign-sequence step,\ndyadic refinement).  A standalone `birthday (x / 2)` axiom\nwould assert more than callers need; this combined form is\nexactly the Conway midpoint recipe and nothing more.\n\nReserved for future induction proofs of the sharper\n`birthday (gonshorIn K s) ≤ s.length` bound; the current\nfile proves the universally-supported `≤ ω` form (see\n`SignSequence.birthday_gonshorIn_le_omega`) and the\n`s.length ≤ 1` cases unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_add_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_add_le","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Birthday is bounded under sum by ordinal natural-sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_neg","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Birthday is symmetric: `b(-x) = b(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_one","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The birthday of one is one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday_zero","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The birthday of zero is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.birthday","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Conway's birthday function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.ofReal_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.ofReal_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The embedding is order-preserving. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.ofReal","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L56-L56","doc":"ℝ-algebra structure: every real number embeds in K. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_right","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L54-L54","doc":"In a strict ordered semiring, we can multiply an inequality `a < b` on the right\nby a positive element `0 < c` to obtain `a * c < b * c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L54-L54","doc":"In a strict ordered semiring, we can multiply an inequality `a < b` on the left\nby a positive element `0 < c` to obtain `c * a < c * b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.mk","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toLinearOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toLinearOrder","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L54-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toZeroLEOneClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toZeroLEOneClass","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L54-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toIsOrderedCancelAddMonoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toIsOrderedCancelAddMonoid","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L54-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toIsStrictOrderedRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toIsStrictOrderedRing","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L54-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField.toField","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L54-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealField","kind":"class","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Basic.lean#L48-L103","doc":"A **surreal-coefficient field** `K` is a linearly ordered field\nextending ℝ, equipped with a Conway-style birthday function.\n\nWe axiomatise rather than construct: the canonical model is\n`K = 𝐍𝐨` (Conway's surreal numbers), but mathlib does not\nyet expose `𝐍𝐨` as a `LinearOrderedField`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}